==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/heitl/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eitl|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|heill|lang=non}} (compare Faroese {{term|heillur|lang=fo}}, Norwegian, Danish, and Swedish {{term|hel|lang=da}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|hailaz|lang=gem-pro}} (compare English {{term|whole|lang=en}}, {{term|hale|lang=en}}, Dutch {{term|heel|lang=nl}}, German {{term|heil|lang=de}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|kóh₂ilus||healthy, whole|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|heil|heilt|heilli|heilastur}}

# [[healthy]]{{jump|is|healthy|s}}
#* [[w:en:Hávamál|Hávamál]] ([[s:en:Poetic Edda/Hávamál|English source]], [[s:is:Hávamál|Icelandic sourve]])
#*: ''Gefendur '''heilir'''!''
#*: ''Gestur er inn kominn!''
#*: ''hvar skal sitja sjá?''
#*: ''Mjög er bráður''
#*: ''sá er á bröndum skal''
#*: ''síns um freista frama.''
#*:: '''Hail''' to the giver! | a guest has come;
#*:: Where shall the stranger sit?
#*:: Swift shall he be who, | with swords shall try
#*:: The proof of his might to make. 
# [[complete]], [[entire]], [[whole]]{{jump|is|whole|s}}
#: ''Þetta tók '''heilt''' ár!''
#:: This took a '''whole''' year!
# [[undamaged]], [[in one piece]]{{jump|is|undamaged|s}}

